6. Conveying Non-Source Forms.

You may convey a covered work in object code form under the terms
of sections 4 and 5, provided that you also convey the
machine-readable Corresponding Source under the terms of this
License, in one of these ways:

a) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by a
fixed, durable copy of the Corresponding Source on a durable
physical medium customarily used for software interchange.

b) Convey the object code in, or embodied in, a physical product
(including a physical distribution medium), accompanied by a
written offer, valid for at least three years and valid for as
long as you offer spare parts or customer service for that product,
to give anyone who possesses the object code either a copy of the
Corresponding Source on a durable physical medium customarily used
for software interchange, or access to copy the Corresponding
Source from a network server at no charge.

c) Convey individual copies of the object code with a copy of the
Corresponding Source on a durable physical medium customarily used
for software interchange. This alternative is allowed only
occasionally and non-commercially, and if you do not offer a
network server, because the cost of providing the Corresponding
Source would exceed the cost of the object code by an amount that
justifies the difference.

d) Convey the object code by offering access from a designated
place (gratis or for a charge), and offer equivalent access to
the Corresponding Source in the same way through the same place at
no charge. If you are a business, you must also offer
equivalent access to the Corresponding Source through a network
server, which you may control. The place of offering may be a
network server that is not publicly accessible. If you are
conveying the object code by offering access through a network
server, you must specify the place of the offer in a way that makes
the object code's availability and the Corresponding Source
convenient for the recipient to obtain it.

e) Convey the object code using peer-to-peer networks, provided
you inform other peers where the Corresponding Source is being
offered to the general public at no charge under this License.

A separable portion of the object code, whose source code is excluded
from the Corresponding Source as a System Interface, need not be
included in the Corresponding Source if the separable portion is
exclusively for the System Interface and its control scripts are
included in the Corresponding Source. This alternative is allowed
only if the separable portion is never conveyed, or is conveyed
without payment for the separable portion, and it is not
exclusively for a System Interface.

